# NIST SP 800-53 Revision 5 — security and privacy controls, with the three
# impact baselines from SP 800-53B.
#
# This is a working copy carried inside ENCLAVE so the tool is useful on first
# run. It covers every base control and the enhancements selected by the
# baselines. For an authorisation package, import the authoritative OSCAL
# catalogue from NIST on the Catalogues page; it replaces this one by id.

@id nist-800-53r5
@name NIST SP 800-53 Revision 5
@version Release 5.1.1
@publisher National Institute of Standards and Technology
@description Security and privacy controls for information systems and organizations, with the low, moderate and high impact baselines from SP 800-53B.
@source https://csrc.nist.gov/pubs/sp/800/53/r5/upd1/final

@profile low = Low impact baseline | Controls selected by SP 800-53B for a low-impact system.
@profile moderate = Moderate impact baseline | Controls selected by SP 800-53B for a moderate-impact system.
@profile high = High impact baseline | Controls selected by SP 800-53B for a high-impact system.
@profile privacy = Privacy control baseline | Controls selected by SP 800-53B where personally identifiable information is processed.

@family AC = Access Control
@family AT = Awareness and Training
@family AU = Audit and Accountability
@family CA = Assessment, Authorization, and Monitoring
@family CM = Configuration Management
@family CP = Contingency Planning
@family IA = Identification and Authentication
@family IR = Incident Response
@family MA = Maintenance
@family MP = Media Protection
@family PE = Physical and Environmental Protection
@family PL = Planning
@family PM = Program Management
@family PS = Personnel Security
@family PT = PII Processing and Transparency
@family RA = Risk Assessment
@family SA = System and Services Acquisition
@family SC = System and Communications Protection
@family SI = System and Information Integrity
@family SR = Supply Chain Risk Management

